/*
 * Declares the CmpCharOperatorValue class.
 *
 * CmpCharOperatorValue represents binary comparison operations applied to two
 * character operands. Character comparisons operate on the underlying code
 * points of the characters, enabling equality and ordering checks. The result
 * of any comparison is always a boolean value.
 *
 * Typical comparisons include:
 *   - equality / inequality,
 *   - relational comparisons(<, <=, >, >=) based on code-point ordering.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::binary::char_::cmp
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/binary/char_/cmp.yr
